<title>NETHERLANDS: KPN sells German unit to Deutsche Post.</title>
<headline>KPN sells German unit to Deutsche Post.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Post and telecommunications group Koninklijke PTT Nederland NV (KPN) said on Thursday it had sold its German unit TNT Netzwerk Logistik (NetLog) to Deutsche Post AG.</p>
<p>NetLog has been handling the transport of parcels for Deutsche Post since 1995, but Deutsche Post cancelled the contract last February when KPN bought NetLog's parent TNT.</p>
<p>KPN fought this decision through a court procedure but it said the present agreement, of which no financial details were disclosed, had settled the conflict.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
